<.shell title="Build a group rule" current={:build_a_group_rule}>
  <h1>Build a group rule</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    An editor inside a page: small inputs and small buttons, since it sits among other content.
  </p>

  <div class="example measure">
    <.rule_editor rows={rule_rows()} options={rule_options()} new_path="#" />
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      A rule is a <a href={page_path(:table)}>table</a>
      of endorsements. A member must hold every one to be in the group.
    </li>
    <li>
      Each endorsement links to its own page, where its qualifications change. A change there
      changes every group that uses it.
    </li>
    <li>The menu adds an endorsement the team already has. New endorsement makes one.</li>
    <li>Done closes the editor. Members change only after you review and send the changes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="spec">
    <code>&lt;.rule_editor rows=&#123;…&#125; options=&#123;…&#125; new_path=&#123;…&#125; /&gt;</code>
    from <code>Web.Components.GroupRule</code>, as on a group's page, with made-up endorsements.
  </p>
</.shell>
